INT. FROSTLINE ARENA - ICE RESURFACER GARAGE - NIGHT

A concrete garage under the stands. Steam from the melt pit. The ice resurfacer idles, humming. A radio on a shelf crackles with the third period.

COACH BRONAGH QUILL, 50s, windbreaker, unlit cigar. SLICK ADEYEMI, 60, resurfacer driver, thermos, headphones around his neck. NEW GUY, 19, goalie pads half on, sits on an upturned bucket and stares at the floor.

ANNOUNCER (V.O.)
(radio)
And the Wolves trail by one with six minutes left.

COACH
Starter's got a broken wrist. You're in.

NEW GUY
I know.

COACH
Say something.

NEW GUY
I don't feel anything.

SLICK
That's the cold.

COACH
That's nerves.

COACH
Slick, wipe the blue line when the horn goes.

SLICK ^
Slick wipes whatever Slick pleases.

Slick offers the thermos. The kid takes it, sips, gags.

NEW GUY
What is that?

SLICK
Coffee and my wife's brandy.

COACH
What's your name, kid? Really. Not "New Guy."

NEW GUY
Finn. Finn Oduya.

COACH
Finn. You ever play in front of eight thousand?

FINN
Four. At a funeral.

SLICK
That's a tougher crowd.

ANNOUNCER (V.O.)
(radio)
And the horn sounds. Two minutes break.

The garage door rumbles. Cold light spills in.

COACH
Go.

Finn stands. Buckles the last strap. Slick fires up the resurfacer. Coach sets the cigar in Finn's glove, like a sacrament.

FINN
I'll bring it back.

COACH
You'll bring a win back.

Finn skates out into the light.
